{
  "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
  "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0000-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We allege that the trustees, through disloyalty and imprudence, caused the trust to lose $750 million."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to quote their brief, that defined-benefit plan participants have no interest in plan assets."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Does your argument depend upon a forward-looking theory of injury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But would they --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JOSHI: Mr. Chief Justice and may it please the Court: When a trustee breaches his fiduciary duties and causes losses to the trust, real"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "money losses, the beneficiary always has been able to sue the trustee for the breach of trust. It's been the law for hundreds of years of trust law and it's expressly in ERISA's text as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Let me propose a hypothetical then about the defined contribution plans. Let's say the trustee is left with discretion. After everybody is paid, if there's extra, you can throw it to somebody, even though it's not in their own contribution plan. So I think you would say the result would be that every single beneficiary could sue, even if all of their investments are clean, for somebody else's defined contribution plan where the -- where the -- where the plan might be dirty; is that right? Does that follow?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Joseph R. PALMORE",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. PALMORE: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: There is no ERISA exception to Article III. Like all plaintiffs in federal court, those with ERISA claims must demonstrate injury. Neither Petitioner here can do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- they're not asking for a distribution to themselves of a surplus. They are asking for a payment to the plan."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Counsel, on that, what if Congress had in its statute -- I know you would disagree that it did this -- what if it had said that every beneficiary has a property interest or a private right to a completely clean trustee. Would that suffice for standing in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The \"no further inquiry\" rule went only to that first question. It said that if the trust engaged in a transaction that was inconsistent with the duty of loyalty or was otherwise prohibited, there would be a presumption of harm to the trust and, therefore, that transaction could be rescinded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We dismissed under 12(b) -- we moved to dismiss under 12(b)(6). That was denied."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "what do you do about the fact that these plans can be\nunderfunded in January and overfunded in\nFebruary and underfunded in March again?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Wouldn't -- wouldn't that theory, taken to its logical\nconclusion, mean that a participant could never sue, a defined-benefit participant or"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Palmore",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the PBGC does -- does -- does matter. It's --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you said, well, can Congress put a property label on anything?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-17-1712",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e8ad065b81e81700654e9dfffc84c790ddf0c23fc9f38a0b425cff129dacf914",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e8ad065b81e8-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 12:11 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
